{
  "id": "ag-linear",
  "chapterNumber": "1",
  "title": {
    "en": "Linear Equations &amp; Lines",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A linear relationship changes at a constant rate — its graph is a straight line. Mastering lines is the foundation for everything from SAT word problems to the slope fields of calculus.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 1.1 — Linear equation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A linear equation in one variable has the form \\( ax+b=0 \\) with \\( a\\neq 0 \\); its single solution is \\( x=-\\dfrac{b}{a} \\). In two variables, \\( y=mx+b \\) describes a line of slope \\( m \\) and \\( y \\)-intercept \\( b \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The slope measures steepness as rise over run, \\( m=\\dfrac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x}=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \\). Drag the sliders to see how \\( m \\) tilts the line and \\( b \\) slides it up or down — the amber dots mark where it crosses the axes.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "lineCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Slope &amp; intercept",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A line y equals m x plus b with adjustable slope and intercept",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "lineDataBtn",
          "panelId": "lineDataPanel",
          "descId": "lineDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "lineDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points along the current line",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "y",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "lineM",
            "label": {
              "en": "Slope &nbsp; <b>m =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -3,
            "max": 3,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 0.1,
            "valueDisplayId": "lineMv",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Slope m",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "lineB",
            "label": {
              "en": "Intercept &nbsp; <b>b =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -4,
            "max": 4,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 0.5,
            "valueDisplayId": "lineBv",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Intercept b",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "lineSlope",
            "label": {
              "en": "slope&nbsp; m",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          },
          {
            "id": "lineYint",
            "label": {
              "en": "y-intercept",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          },
          {
            "id": "lineXint",
            "label": {
              "en": "x-intercept",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          }
        ],
        "equationDisplay": {
          "id": "lineEq",
          "value": "y = x + 1",
          "style": "font-size:.9rem; padding:9px 11px; background:var(--paper-2); border-radius:8px"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "heading": "Three forms of a line",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Slope–intercept",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( y=mx+b \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Point–slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( y-y_1=m\\,(x-x_1) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Standard",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( Ax+By=C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.A — Solve",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( 3x+5=20 \\).</p><p>Subtract 5, then divide by 3:</p>\\[ 3x=15 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x=5. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.B — Equation of a line",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the line through \\( (1,2) \\) and \\( (5,10) \\).</p><p>Slope first, then point–slope with \\( (1,2) \\):</p>\\[ m=\\frac{10-2}{5-1}=2, \\qquad y-2=2(x-1)\\;\\Longrightarrow\\; y=2x. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
